   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2022-02-17",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The bill amends the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act to allow corrective services authorities to access telecommunications data to combat illicit mobile phone use in prisons, implementing a recommendation from the comprehensive review of the national intelligence community's legal framework. A temporary declaration under section 176A has already given Corrective Services NSW this access, and Operation Ironside has resulted in over 350 individuals being charged."
  }
 ],
